{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-ratio-predictions","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:mass-ratio-predictions","kind":"remark","title":"Theoretical mass ratios from the mass identity","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-topological-mass-formula"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-topological-mass-formula","tags":["mass","prediction","observation"],"text":"mass-ratio-predictions.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:mass-ratio-predictions\"></a><p>The <a href=\"#def:mass-identity\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-mass-identity\">mass identity</a> expresses inertial mass as the norm of a nonabelian multiplicative integral over a surface bounding the vortex filament. In the Descartes universe (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi(\\mathcal{S}) = -6</code>), bundle topology constrains vortex configurations and determines the mass spectrum. Evaluating the mass identity at successive levels of the brane tower (<a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>) yields mass ratio predictions.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/mass-ratio-predictions.md","heading":"Remark","number":"17.5.6","page":"b/rem-mass-ratio-predictions","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
